    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A great principality of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#france">France</a>, ruled by the Raymondine counts of Toulouse from the ninth century until 1271.</li><li>Its courts patronised the troubadours, and Count Raymond IV led a major army on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#first-crusade">First Crusade</a> that founded the County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#tripoli">Tripoli</a>.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a> against the Cathars broke the counts, and the county passed to the French crown in 1271.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Simon de Montfort, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a>, was killed in 1218 by a stone from a siege engine outside Toulouse; an Occitan chronicle says women of the city worked the machine.</p></aside>
    </section>

